<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Chola Empire</h1><p class="st-meta">848 CE – 1279 CE (approx.) · capital Thanjavur</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The South Indian empire of Rajaraja and Rajendra, whose navy reached Southeast Asia and whose temples and bronzes are masterpieces of Indian art.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 848 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayalaya-chola">Vijayalaya</a>, a local chief descended from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/early-cholas">Early Cholas</a>, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thanjavur">Thanjavur</a> in the Kaveri delta. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aditya-i">Aditya I</a> defeated the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/pallava-dynasty">Pallava dynasty</a> around 897, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parantaka-i">Parantaka I</a> conquered the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/first-pandyan-empire">First Pandyan Empire</a>. After a setback against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/rashtrakuta-dynasty">Rashtrakutas</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajaraja-i">Rajaraja I</a>, from 985, made the Cholas the greatest power of the south.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajaraja-i">Rajaraja I</a> conquered northern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-maldives">Maldives</a> and built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brihadishvara-temple">Brihadishvara</a> temple at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thanjavur">Thanjavur</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajendra-chola-i">Rajendra I</a> marched to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges</a>, founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gangaikondacholapuram">Gangaikondacholapuram</a> and launched a naval raid on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srivijaya">Srivijaya</a> in 1025. Villages were run by assemblies, recorded in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttaramerur">Uttaramerur</a> inscriptions, and land was carefully surveyed for revenue. Chola bronzes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nataraja">Shiva Nataraja</a> and Tamil devotional literature flourished, and merchant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guild">guilds</a> traded with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song China</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>From the late 12th century the empire was squeezed by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/hoysala-empire">Hoysala Empire</a> and a revived <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pandya-dynasty">Pandya</a> kingdom. In 1279 the last Chola king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajendra-chola-iii">Rajendra III</a>, was defeated by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/later-pandyan-empire">Pandyas</a>, and Chola rule ended.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/chola-empire.jpg" alt="Chola Empire" width="320" height="188"><figcaption>Image: Nikel3012 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chola_Empire_Map_(1).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>848 CE – 1279 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Thanjavur</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Rajaraja I, Rajendra I, Kulottunga I</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Shaivism, Vaishnavism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Tamil, Sanskrit</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a>, <a href="/countries/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a>, <a href="/countries/maldives">Maldives</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Chola dynasty, Medieval Cholas, Cholas, Imperial Cholas</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1064&amp;focus=chola-empire" aria-label="Chola Empire on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6867 1760 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Chola Empire lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7187 2016L7783 2219M7187 